# Build context rules for the API image, which builds from the repository root
# (`docker build -f api/Dockerfile .`) because it has to copy both `api/` and
# the top-level `products/catalog/`. Replaces the former `api/.dockerignore`,
# which no longer applies now that the context is not `api/`.
#
# The UI and Keycloak images still build from their own directories and use
# their own ignore files, so nothing here affects them.

# Start from nothing and re-include only what the API image needs. An allowlist
# rather than a denylist because the context otherwise pulls in `var/pg_data`,
# which the build cannot read, and `.claude/worktrees`, which contains whole
# copies of the repository.
*
!api
!products/catalog

# Within those, the junk the old api/.dockerignore excluded.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/*.so
**/.Python
**/.eggs
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/venv
**/ENV
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/dist
**/build
**/*.md
**/docs
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/.env.*
